{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nSeventeen store-interface files contain 56 audited prose blocks. Scope was revalidated on `origin/main@0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e`; stable anchors replace stale or block-cutting ranges.\n\n## Approach\nCondense only anchored comments and true leading docstrings in Scope. Preserve every non-docstring runtime string, constant, regex, fixture value, subprocess argument, decorator, assertion, and executable statement.\n\nParse immutable before/final blobs with `type_comments=True`; remove only leading docstrings from modules, classes, functions, and async functions; normalize `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; and require the remaining ASTs to match. Restrict comment edits to anchored blocks and adjacent blank lines. Compare directives and shebangs byte-for-byte.\n\n## Scope\n- `sync_contention_harness.py` module docstring — retain the shared harness, the need for `_clear_sync_throttle`, and bare-import fixture topology.\n- `test_atomic_ticket_dir_create_021d.py` module docstring — retain atomic publication, no-debris behavior, and interruption at the write-lock boundary.\n- `test_event_append_transient_retry.py` module; blocks bound to the three stderr constants; and docstrings for commit-ODB retry, index-add retry, orphan-lock healing, and cross-path healing — retain exact classifier signatures and pre/post-ref retry boundaries.\n- `test_execution_mode_dispatch.py` single-turn test docstring and blocks bound to the cache, proxy-bypass, and no-build-provider stubs — retain optional-import isolation, keyword-only mode, ambient-proxy isolation, and provider-session behavior.\n- `test_git_contention_9305.py` module and concurrent-process test docstrings — retain local-lock absorption, own-pathspec commits, and the two-process observable.\n- `test_inline_write_push.py` module and detached-upkeep test docstrings — retain inline-writer inventory and the no-detached-mutator precondition.\n- `test_llm_optionality.py` module, `_gate_source_local`, operation/fail-safe blocks, named fail-safe/missing-extra/matrix docstrings, and the anchored fixture/assertion blocks — retain lazy imports, local-source necessity, raised versus structured degradation, exhaustive discovery, and childless seed reachability.\n- `test_pass1_fanout_gate_session.py` module, `GateCheckingRunner`, and fanout test docstrings — retain that raw threads need explicit gate-context propagation.\n- `test_push_shared_stash_2fa6.py` module docstring — retain repo-global stash semantics, the interleaving race, SHA-addressed restore, and unchanged `refs/stash`.\n- `test_reads_under_sync_contention.py` module, deadline-bound comments, two named test docstrings, and their product-deadline/hang-guard blocks — retain complete-or-loud reads and distinct in-process/subprocess bounds.\n- `test_reconcile_workflow_no_shallow_rebase.py` module and explicit-fetch-ref test docstrings — retain full-history merge and destination refspecs.\n- `test_reconciler_apply_bindings.py` module docstring — retain current `runtime.compose_reconciler_runtime` ownership, one composed runtime, and transport forwarding.\n- `test_reconciler_operation_bindings.py` module docstring — retain the public seam, frozen scope, selected-provider-only construction, transport seam, and secret boundaries.\n- `test_review_as_workflow.py` module docstring — retain executor bridging and all three active equivalence/public-entry nodes.\n- `test_review_regressions.py` module docstring — retain rollback, index cleanup, and tracker-root consistency.\n- `test_show_no_stall.py` module and one-round burst block — retain the short reconverge deadline, complete-or-error result, and detection-floor rationale.\n- `test_txn_transient_retry.py` module docstring — retain retry of pre-ref `could not parse HEAD` failures and immediate failure for non-transient errors.\n\nConsumers include pytest; store fixtures and contention suites; workflow/optionality CI; reconciler shape checks; documentation; and `check_comment_hygiene.py`. No runtime docstring reader was found.\n\nPreserve `# type: ignore[override]` on `GateCheckingRunner.run` and `# type: ignore[arg-type]` in `test_dirty_merge_recovery_ignores_a_foreign_stash`, byte-exact and attached.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Only scoped comments, true leading docstrings, or adjacent blank lines change; normalized AST equality passes.\n- [ ] Runtime values, assertions, decorators, and executable statements remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Every directive remains byte-identical and attached to the same statement.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter and removes repetition, history, ornament, or obvious narration.\n- [ ] A non-author reviewer posts one leaf-linked TSV row per edited block with immutable before/final citations, preserved contract/consumer, before/after words, and both verdicts.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records `semantic-preservation=PASS` and `bloat-removal=PASS`; missing or failing rows block closure.\n- [ ] The normalized guard, focused tests, two contention-harness consumer nodes, comment-hygiene check, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify` pass.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded normalized-AST/allowlist/directive comparator; the 17 impacted files plus both `test_bridge_preview_under_sync_contention_heldout.py` preview-bound nodes; `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`; path-scoped `git diff --check`; and `make verify`. The independent TSV is authoritative for prose quality."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788616534493062001,"uuid":"ab24c6f9-0d08-488a-9f86-f4dc899446e4"}